Let the sink-list frames clip their rows.

Each GtkListBox sits in a GtkFrame that draws a rounded border. In GTK4 a
widget's children are not clipped to its border-radius unless its "overflow"
property is hidden, so the rows painted their own corners straight over the
frame's -- visible wherever the theme gives a row a different radius than the
frame, which a pill row always does.

Setting overflow=hidden makes the frame clip, so the corners agree by
construction whatever radius the theme picks. Applied to all four lists; the
connect, streaming and error pages have the same frame.

Not upstreamed.

--- a/src/nd-window.ui
+++ b/src/nd-window.ui
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
                                             </child>
                                             <child>
                                               <object class="GtkFrame">
+                                                <property name="overflow">hidden</property>
                                                 <child>
                                                   <object class="GtkListBox" id="find_sink_list"/>
                                                 </child>
@@ -148,6 +149,7 @@
                                 </child>
                                 <child>
                                   <object class="GtkFrame">
+                                    <property name="overflow">hidden</property>
                                     <child>
                                       <object class="GtkListBox" id="connect_sink_list"/>
                                     </child>
@@ -216,6 +218,7 @@
                                 </child>
                                 <child>
                                   <object class="GtkFrame">
+                                    <property name="overflow">hidden</property>
                                     <child>
                                       <object class="GtkListBox" id="stream_sink_list"/>
                                     </child>
@@ -284,6 +287,7 @@
